ills. West 20 to 30 mph\nwith gusts up to 50 mph on the plains.\n\n* RELATIVE HUMIDITY...Between 10 to 20 percent.\n\n* IMPACTS...Conditions will be favorable for rapid fire spread. Avoid\noutdoor burning and any activity that may produce a spark and start\na wildfire.","ends":"2026-11-18T16:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Larimer and Boulder Counties Between 6000 and 9000 Feet; Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Central and South Weld County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.382bc923e46a867f01f5d73980c813cffc84cd48.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.382bc923e46a867f01f5d73980c813cffc84cd48.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-11-18T00:07:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 180007 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 507 PM MST Tue Nov 17 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - First wind event of the season likely (>70%) for the northern Front Range mountains and foothills late tonight into Wednesday. Gusts of 60-75 mph with isolated stronger gusts possible. - Brief potential for wind gusts of 40-50 mph and isolated stronger win","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-11-17T22:00:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Tonight through Sunday... Breezy southeast winds have developed this afternoon, mainly for areas south of I-76. Smoke dispersal is fair to good across most of the area with the central and northern plains having poor dispersal. Winds increase late tonight and Wednesday morning as a storm system passes north of Colorado. This system is expected to bring light snow to the northern moun","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"stati